        {
          "id": 802114018,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Yes. I think that the pcre-devel requirement is unnecessary (which is why it's commented out) since `glib2-devel` requires `pcre-devel` on every distribution I'm familiar with, but leaving it in there commented out is reasonable.\n\nThere's a similar chain with pcre2-devel - we require it now, but glib2-devel requires libselinux-devel which requires pcre2-devel on most distributions. Actually I think I'll just add pcre2-devel as a BuildRequires anyway, since it is required now to build.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
